# Universal Ctags options for mod_auth_openidc.
#
# This file used to synthesize tags for the config accessors that cfg/ generates with
# token-pasting macros (oidc_cfg_provider_issuer_get, oidc_cmd_dir_pass_claims_as_set, ...), by
# matching each generator's CALL site with a regex and reassembling the name it would produce.
#
# Those rules are gone: they were wrong often enough to mislead. Measured against the compiled
# tree they emitted 91 accessor names that do not exist -- 68 of which appear nowhere in the
# sources at all -- while missing 82 that do. The whole cfg/cache.c family was mis-tagged, because
# that generator prepends "cache_" to the member name and the regex could not know: it produced
# oidc_cfg_shm_size_max_get for what is really oidc_cfg_cache_shm_size_max_get. Reconstructing a
# macro's output with a regex cannot be made reliable; each new generator variant is a new way to
# be wrong.
#
# The compiler knows the answer, so it is asked instead:
#
#     make -C src cfgtags        # writes src/cfgtags
#
# See src/cfg/gen-tags.sh. Use it alongside an ordinary index, which covers everything else:
#
#     ctags -R src/
#     vim ':set tags=./tags,./src/cfgtags'
#
# Nothing else here needs special handling, so no options are set.
